\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Overview of PyTT. A fixed call graph orders function analysis. For each function, Context-free Code Simplification supplies shared facts to PSTC Generation. A PSTC contains entry assertions ($P$), ordered path behavior, and exit assertions ($Q$). Type conflicts enter Type Conflict Analysis, which expands relevant callee paths and re-infers the resulting trace. Revised path contracts update callee PSTCs and dependent callers.}}{6}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-overview}{{2}{6}{Overview of PyTT. A fixed call graph orders function analysis. For each function, Context-free Code Simplification supplies shared facts to PSTC Generation. A PSTC contains entry assertions ($P$), ordered path behavior, and exit assertions ($Q$). Type conflicts enter Type Conflict Analysis, which expands relevant callee paths and re-infers the resulting trace. Revised path contracts update callee PSTCs and dependent callers}{figure.caption.8}{}}
